.Dd October 14, 2026
.Dt FORTI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm forti
.Nd FortiOS from the command line
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar global-options
.Ar command
.Op Ar arguments
.Nm
.Cm configure
.Op Fl -profile Ar name Fl -host Ar host Op Ar options
.Nm
.Cm doctor
.Op Fl -profile Ar name
.Nm
.Cm get
.Ar resource
.Op Ar key
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads and changes FortiGate configuration through the FortiOS REST API.
It works with
.Em profiles :
named connection settings for a device, kept in
.Pa config.json
together with a reference to the device's API key.
The key itself is kept in the secret store, an environment variable or a command's output, never in
the configuration file and never on the command line.
.Pp
Text output is meant for people; with
.Fl -json
every command prints a stable JSON envelope,
.Dl {\(dqok\(dq: true, \(dqdata\(dq: ..., \(dqmeta\(dq: {...}}
or
.Dl {\(dqok\(dq: false, \(dqerror\(dq: {\(dqcode\(dq: ..., \(dqmessage\(dq: ..., \(dqdetails\(dq: {...}}}
and the exit status follows the error code (see
.Sx EXIT STATUS ) .
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options may appear before or after the command.
.Bl -tag -width "-p, --profile name"
.It Fl p , Fl -profile Ar name
Use this profile.
The default is the default profile, or the only one.
.It Fl -vdom Ar name
VDOM for this request.
.It Fl -json
Print the JSON result envelope.
Also
.Ev FORTI_OUTPUT Ns =json .
.It Fl -no-color
No ANSI colors.
Colors are used only when the output is a terminal and
.Ev NO_COLOR
is unset.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Help for
.Nm
or for a command.
.It Fl -version
Print the version and the FortiOS version the models were generated from.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss Setup
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm configure
Create or update a profile.
Without options it prompts on the terminal; the API key is typed with echo disabled.
With options it runs without prompts:
.Bl -tag -width "--api-key-command cmd"
.It Fl -profile Ar name
Profile name (letters, digits,
.Ql -
and
.Ql _ ) .
Required with other options.
.It Fl -host Ar host
Host name or address, without scheme or port.
.It Fl -port Ar n
Admin HTTPS port (default 443).
.It Fl -vdom Ar name
Default VDOM for the profile.
.It Fl -ca-bundle Ar path
PEM CA bundle that verifies the device certificate.
.It Fl -resolve-ip Ar ip
Connect to this address while verifying the certificate for
.Ar host .
.It Fl -client-cert Ar path
PKCS#12 client certificate.
.It Fl -api-key-stdin
Read the API key from standard input and keep it in the secret store.
.It Fl -api-key-env Ar var
Read the key from the environment variable
.Ar var
on every use; only the name is saved.
.It Fl -api-key-command Ar cmd
Run
.Ar cmd
(split like a shell, executed without one) and use the first line of its output.
.It Fl -cert-password-stdin , Fl -cert-password-env Ar var , Fl -cert-password-command Ar cmd
The client certificate's password, from the same kinds of source.
.It Fl -mode Ar mode
.Cm read-only
(default),
.Cm guarded
or
.Cm autonomous ;
see
.Sx OPERATING MODES .
.It Fl -default
Make this the default profile.
.It Fl -skip-check
Save without contacting the device.
.El
.Pp
Before saving,
.Cm configure
reads
.Pa monitor/system/status
from the device.
If the read fails nothing is saved.
An authentication failure is not retried, because FortiOS locks out an API user after repeated
failures.
.It Cm profile Op Cm list
List profiles; the default is marked with
.Ql * .
.Cm devices
is a short form.
.It Cm profile show Op Ar name
Show a profile and where its key comes from (never the key).
.It Cm profile default Ar name
Make
.Ar name
the default profile.
.It Cm profile mode Oo Ar name Oc Ar mode
Set the operating mode.
.It Cm profile remove Ar name
Delete the profile and its stored secrets.
.It Cm doctor
Run ordered checks: configuration directory and file modes, profile, secret resolution, CA bundle
and client certificate files, connection (DNS, TCP, TLS), authentication, FortiOS version against
the SDK schema, operating mode (for autonomous profiles also the API account's privileges), and whether
.Nm forti-mcp
is on
.Ev PATH .
Each is reported as ok, warn, fail, skip or info.
Exits 0 when nothing failed, otherwise with the status of the first failure.
.El
.Ss Read
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm devices
List profiles.
.It Cm discover Op Ar search | resource
Search the resource catalog, or show a resource's attributes
.Pq Fl -kind , Fl -fields , Fl -live , Fl -start , Fl -count .
.It Cm get Ar resource Op Ar key
Read configuration or monitor data
.Pq Fl -filter , Fl -fields , Fl -start , Fl -count , Fl -param .
Device secrets are shown as
.Dq <redacted> ;
.Fl -reveal
shows them on a terminal, or with
.Fl -json .
.El
.Ss Changes and integrations
.Cm plan ,
.Cm apply
and
.Cm install
are described by
.Nm
.Ar command
.Fl -help .
.Sh OPERATING MODES
The FortiOS account's privileges are the primary authorization boundary.
A profile's mode is the operator's policy on top of it:
.Bl -tag -width autonomous
.It Cm read-only
Reads and plan previews only; every apply is refused.
The default.
.It Cm guarded
A change is applied only after a person approves the exact plan with
.Nm
.Cm plan approve Ar id .
.It Cm autonomous
Changes are applied without interactive approval.
The agent can do anything the API account may do.
Validation, drift checks, verification, audit records and rollback plans still apply.
Scope the account's admin profile and trusted hosts to what the agent should manage.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width FORTI_SECRET_STORE
.It Ev FORTI_CONFIG_DIR
Configuration directory (default
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/forti ,
else
.Pa ~/.config/forti ) .
.It Ev FORTI_STATE_DIR
Plans, approvals and the audit log (default
.Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/forti ,
else
.Pa ~/.local/state/forti ) .
.It Ev FORTI_CACHE_DIR
Cached live schemas (default
.Pa $XDG_CACHE_HOME/forti ,
else
.Pa ~/.cache/forti ) .
.It Ev FORTI_SECRET_STORE
.Cm file
or
.Cm keychain .
Default: the macOS Keychain on macOS, the file store elsewhere.
.It Ev FORTI_OUTPUT
.Cm json
prints the JSON envelope for every command.
.It Ev NO_COLOR
Disables colors.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/forti/config.json
Profiles; mode 0600 in a 0700 directory.
Contains no secrets.
.It Pa ~/.config/forti/credentials/
The file secret store: one 0600 file per secret.
.It Login Keychain, service Dq forti
The macOS secret store, accounts
.Ar profile Ns /api-key
and
.Ar profile Ns /cert-password .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 3n -compact
.It 0
success
.It 1
internal error
.It 2
usage error
.It 3
configuration: missing or invalid profile, credentials or config file
.It 4
connection (DNS, connect, TLS, timeout) or authentication (HTTP 401/403)
.It 5
not found: unknown object or resource
.It 6
validation or other FortiOS error
.It 7
refused: read-only mode, missing approval, or stale plan
.It 8
partial failure or unknown outcome of a change
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Configure a device, check it, and read its firewall policy:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
forti configure
forti doctor
forti get firewall/policy --fields policyid,name,action,status
.Ed
.Pp
Configure from a password manager without prompts:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
op read op://ops/fw01/api-key | forti configure --profile fw01 \e
    --host fw01.example.net --ca-bundle ~/fw01-ca.pem --api-key-stdin
.Ed
.Sh SECURITY
TLS certificate verification is always on; no option disables it.
Use
.Fl -ca-bundle
for self-signed or private-CA devices, and
.Fl -resolve-ip
to connect to an address while verifying the certificate's name.
Secrets are never accepted as arguments and never printed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr forti-mcp 1
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/valkyrianlabs/forti-cli
